WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:09.086
In this video, you will add a whole list of homes to your contest yourself, for example when your city already collects registrations somewhere else.

00:00:09.086 --> 00:00:10.090
We start on the map.

00:00:11.049 --> 00:00:12.723
Start at SoCal Lights dot app.

00:00:15.584 --> 00:00:18.134
On the home page, tap Use my location.

00:00:19.944 --> 00:00:20.924
Then tap Allow.

00:00:25.416 --> 00:00:28.623
Now look at the top of the map, beside the search box.

00:00:28.623 --> 00:00:31.406
See your picture, or your initial, in a circle?

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:35.969
That is your account menu, and it is the doorway to everything else on the site.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:36.671
Tap it.

00:00:38.211 --> 00:00:40.170
In the menu, tap Your contests.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.817
That is where the contests you run, and the homes you entered, live.

00:00:45.817 --> 00:00:47.699
Tap Mine, your personal page.

00:00:49.254 --> 00:00:51.362
Tap Manage, next to your contest.

00:00:53.196 --> 00:00:54.390
Now tap Entries.

00:00:56.099 --> 00:00:58.735
Homes can be added here until voting starts.

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:01.551
Open Add homes yourself.

00:01:01.551 --> 00:01:06.301
Each home goes straight onto the ballot and the routes, with no photo, and no sign in.

00:01:07.961 --> 00:01:14.156
Paste one home per line: the street address, city and ZIP, then a bar, and the family name.

00:01:14.156 --> 00:01:16.691
The city, ZIP and name are optional.

00:01:17.545 --> 00:01:20.003
Paste your list, up to a hundred at a time.

00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:23.312
Tap Check addresses.

00:01:25.353 --> 00:01:27.889
This looks up each address, and adds nothing yet.

00:01:28.782 --> 00:01:30.195
Found means ready.

00:01:30.195 --> 00:01:33.410
Not found means a typo, so fix it and check again.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:35.507
Already in means it is in your contest.

00:01:36.343 --> 00:01:41.565
Tick the box to confirm that the residents agreed to have their address shown on the public map.

00:01:43.256 --> 00:01:45.681
The button now says how many homes it will add.

00:01:45.681 --> 00:01:47.105
Tap Add 3 homes.

00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:55.519
The three homes that were found are on the map and the ballot, tagged Added by organizer.

00:01:55.519 --> 00:01:58.758
The two that were not found stay in the box, so you can fix them.

00:01:59.726 --> 00:02:01.023
Added one by mistake?

00:02:01.023 --> 00:02:01.978
Tap Remove.

00:02:03.575 --> 00:02:05.180
Then tap again to confirm.

00:02:07.051 --> 00:02:09.958
That is how you put a whole neighborhood on the ballot.

00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:12.347
Homes can be added until voting starts.

00:02:13.688 --> 00:02:16.489
Next up: Edit your contest and change the dates.
